# How detekt finds Rolabox's rules. detekt has no list of rule sets to configure: it looks in every jar
# on its `detektPlugins` classpath for a file with exactly this name (Java's ServiceLoader), and
# loads the class named on each line. Without this file the rules compile and their tests pass, but
# detekt never runs them, and the `rolabox:` block in config/detekt/detekt.yml does nothing.
com.eduardoflores.rolabox.detekt.RolaboxRuleSetProvider
